#passage(("I'm not really asking about the people; I'm more asking about truth and falsehood, because what matters is what is true. When you die, where are you going to end? Is the right answer to say \"I hope\", or to actually have an idea of where you going to end up?", "I don't believe there's such thing as \"I'm religious\" or \"I'm not religious\". You're a human in the end, and you will die one day, whether you want to call yourself religious or non-religious. The fact is, death comes to everyone. And when you say \"later on\", it assumes that you know when you're going to die. If you know people who died younger than you, who gave you a guarantee you live longer? So if you're a person who cares about truth, and believes truth is a valuable thing, and intelligent enough to understand that what matters is what comes later, not what is happening today, you'll start doing your investigation.", "There are some nice people as Christians, there are some nice people as [Sikhs], there are some nice people as Hindus; doesn't make Hinduism the truth. So we've got to investigate that religion itself, and through investigation you'll come to the conclusion whether this is true.", "You don't determine where people end up; I don't. Who determines? Of course God determines, the one who created. The Creator who made you is the one who determines [where] you will end up. Because if there is heaven and hell, then who created heaven and hell? God. If God created heaven and hell, he determines who enters and who doesn't enter. He's going to do what he wants to do.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Truth Seeking Sikh Encounters A Muslim! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mSQiGa_P9bY", ((14, "0:14–0:46"), (48, "0:48–1:22"), (86, "1:26–1:38"), (114, "1:54–2:21"),), id: 884)
