et. Moses was a Muslim prophet. Abraham was a Muslim prophet. All of them were Muslims. But people later on changed the teachings of these messengers and prophets. And due to that, you cannot follow something corrupted by humans and leave the ultimate truth that is there from God. So we're talking about following. We're not talking about that there is other religions that exist or they don't exist.", "I wasn't saying about reading what other people have to offer. I was saying following what other people have to offer. I talk to Christians and I quote their scriptures to them. I talk to Jewish people and I quote the scriptures to them. Talk to Hindus and I quote the scriptures to them. Why? Because I've read these scriptures. I know what they say. It's not about reading what other religions say or they don't say. I'm talking about following. So, if you become Muslim, you don't become close-minded or anything. You find the truth.", "If you know for a fact there's 10,000 books in front of you, all of them are how to swim. You know for a fact that one book is the book that is perfect, from the best swimmer in the world. That is going to be the best and fastest, most efficient way, most perfect way of learning how to swim. And you know that every single other book that exists out there doesn't have the right way of swimming. So if you do it, you might get muscle pain, you might get dislocated muscles, you might get issues. Would you read that book only, and stick to it, and follow it, [ignoring] all of these books? These books exist. They exist, but they're not for your benefit. You can spend your time reading them, no problem. They're not going to increase you anything when it comes to beneficial knowledge, when it comes to what you should and shouldn't do. Everything in Islam, not just the alcohol, every teaching, from what you can eat, from what you can dress, from how you behave, every single thing in Islam is perfect.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Rational Thinker Asks 