#passage(("The details of the attributes of God, or the rest of the attributes of God, we know through Revelation. What we do is: first we establish the existence of a higher power, Creator, or the attributes that we were discussing, like the power, the independency, all of that. Then, once that is the case, we investigate the claims of these prophets and Messengers, and the Revelation they came with, and we see: does it actually show Divinity, as they would claim, that it comes from a Divine Source, or does it not show Divinity? And based on that, we believe that these are the attributes of God.", "So when it comes to Prophet Muhammad, for example: we know that humans, or living beings here, do not know the future. We know that we're limited by that time space. So we say: if you look at Prophet Muhammad, he spoke about the future in detail: what's happening at his time, 200 years after him, it's happening today, 1,400 years later. And he didn't say it's my knowledge. He said no one knows the Unseen except God, but God revealed some of this information and knowledge as an Evidence as well, to show the people that this is coming from the Creator, it's coming from God. So that's one evidence.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Atheist Examines The Muslim Belief In God! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aymar_bEYMg", ((822, "13:42–14:18"), (859, "14:19–14:56"),), id: 898)
