#passage(("Why is the Bible not from God? The Bible is not from God for the following reasons. Number one, it's not preserved, which means that humans have added their own words into the scripture. We no longer know what is attributed to Jesus and what is not attributed to Jesus, what anonymous authors have written, and that is being agreed upon by Christian textual criticism scholars. Reason number two, the book contains contradictions. God, the creator of the universe, does not allow contradictions. He's not going to make a contradiction: he says something, and then he says the opposite of it in a different place, like he doesn't know what he said before. That's from humans, and therefore that makes it man-made. Number three, it contradicts the world externally. We've realized, when we've studied, when we advanced, that things that are written in this book are not really applicable to the reality.", "So when I make a claim that the Bible is not from God, I give reason. But you can't say the Quran [isn't from] God because some people wrote it. Someone can write something and it can still be from God at the same time. That's not a contradiction.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Buddhist Gets Defensive After A Muslim Highlights The Problems With Buddhism! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cCyN0gL4kEI", ((2688, "44:48–45:36"), (2736, "45:36–45:50"),), id: 935)
