#passage(("The important point is this: all these religions agree on certain attributes of God, like that God is All Powerful, All Knowing, Merciful, Just, Wise. These are all attributes that all religions agree upon. Also these religions make claims. What you have to do to find out which religion is The Truth is that you investigate and you test these religions one by one.", "This criteria can be applied to any Scripture, in order for you to know it's from God or not. It has to be free from errors and contradictions, because God does not contradict himself. The world has no physical contradictions on a macro level that we see with our eyes, and God is All Knowing by definition, by agreement of all of those religions, so he can not be contradicting himself. And also the Scripture has to be [preserved] from the source, whatever that source is. If the scripture comes from 100 years ago, it has to be preserved from that time; 1000 years ago, it has to be preserved from that time; 10000 years, we need to have it from that time. We need to have a way to come back to the source.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Agnostic Challenges Muslim On God Then This Happens! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MSk1AiEaXH8", ((195, "3:15–3:29"), (214, "3:34–4:14"),), id: 936)
