#passage(("If it is from God, I'm trying to follow God. Therefore, God will preserve His Message. The last thing in my criteria is that Scripture need to have some sort of evidence that substantiate that it's from God: something that you cannot imitate, that that Prophet or Messenger did, which shows he's breaking the natural laws that we know.", "Now, I would guarantee you no other Scripture would go through this criteria and go to the other side except Islam. Other religions, all of them will be falsified by this criteria: Hinduism, Christianity, Judaism, whatever religion you want. You'll find contradictions in the Scripture, internal and external contradictions; you'll find that there is no Scripture preserved from the time of the origin; you'll find they have no substantiated evidence that they can show you, that is objective, that shows you it's from God.", "Islam is the only religion that will pass all of these tests, that has a Scripture that is preserved from the time. It has no contradictions. And clearly there are so many evidence that are in The Quran that shows that this cannot be from Prophet Muhammad or from any human being. For example, The Quran talking about the future; The Quran talking about the naturalistic world, things naturalistic that are happening and that we're learning today through science; The Quran is talking about Ancient History that we did not have access to, because we do not have the language to read these Manuscripts to begin with. The Quran has all of these type of evidences, that if anyone were to investigate or look at, he would have to come to the necessary conclusion that this has to be from God.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Why Does God Not Communicate With Humans? Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1c92faSXNec", ((585, "9:45–10:41"), (656, "10:56–11:23"), (691, "11:31–12:12"),), id: 937)
