#passage(("Anyone can be wrong. I can be wrong. Nobody knows everything. But you can know certain things to be true. I know 1 plus 1 equals two. Nobody's going to come and tell me you're wrong about 1 plus 1 equals 2. It is true. We know as human beings that this is something, as common sense, that is true.", "The scripture cannot have internal or external contradictions. Meaning, if something comes from God as revelation, it doesn't contradict itself. God does not contradict himself, nor does he contradict the world. He created everything. You have this law of non-contradiction: you don't have a married bachelor; you don't have a square circle. Things work in harmony. What do I mean by internal, external? Internal meaning: scripture cannot say 1 plus 1 equals 1, and you read later in the scripture it says 1 plus 1 equals 2. Then we have a contradiction there, because it's saying two statements that cannot be reconciled, and is contradicting its own self in the scripture. Number two, it cannot contradict the external reality: what we observe with our own eyes.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “The Muslim Lantern, Sneako and Arab Debate Religion! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QiBVA3ZecoI", ((928, "15:28–15:42"), (986, "16:26–17:24"),), id: 938)
