#passage(("I'm talking about world religions, not talking about small religions. We're talking about religions where, if you want to count the population of the planet, you can say more than a third of the population, or half of the population if you count Hinduism and Christianity only. So many people are following this. So when someone says \"how do I know the religion of truth?\", it's not really as hard as people make it seem. What matters is the investigation that you put into that.", "Of course, we know the Quran mentions this idea, that the Quran has No contradictions. And if you are someone coming with a false religion, you wouldn't even put that criteria. Why risk it? Why even mention this? It's like you're encouraging people, you're putting a challenge: if this wasn't from God, you'll find [many] contradictions. You'll be encouraged to go and do your research. So here's the challenge we put today, is going to remain until the day of judgment: go find us a contradiction in the Quran. You're not going to find it. The revelation of Allah is perfected, as [Allah] says.", "Now, another criteria, another thing which is a necessity for a religion to be from God: preservation. That faith and that religion has to be preserved in the original form that it was in. Why is that a criteria for a religion to be from God?", "Let's say God revealed something to me, and I have a religion. God revealed to me: be good to your mother, give charity, whatever commands they are. I write them down. Ten commandments: get my own ten commandments. Go buy cereal in the morning, whatever the command is. Then I pass away, I die. Now I have followers of my religion. I told you guys: you guys are the followers. You know what to do now. Everybody has the ten commandments. I die. Then one of the people here comes and then starts to change: give 50% of your money to this guy, command number one; don't park your car in front of the masjid, command number two; and just change them to whatever absurdities they are.", "Then that's it. What God communicated to us is no longer there. Even if he just changes one command or two commands, you don't know what is from God and what is not from God. The minute there's a corruption in a scripture, the minute there's a corruption of the communication that is supposed to come from God to us, we cannot trust it. And if we cannot trust it, then how can we follow it?",), "The Muslim Lantern, “How Do You Know Which Religion Is From God? A Detailed Comprehensive Analysis | The Muslim Lantern”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9F5gS1yWIRI", ((1135, "18:55–19:23"), (1163, "19:23–20:00"), (1200, "20:00–20:32"), (1237, "20:37–21:24"), (1284, "21:24–21:44"),), id: 942)
