#passage(("The Christians would say that everything in the Bible is true and anything that is outside the Bible is false. And they would say: when the Quran says, for example, that Moses is a prophet from God, the Quran is true; it's right in this verse. So, it's the same thing.", "It applies to any faith that you want to look at anyways, so it's not a critique to Islam, because every ideology would follow what they believe is true and, of course, would reject something that they don't believe is true. Now, when it comes to Islam, why do we say it works for Islam and it doesn't works for any other ideology? Number one, we have proof and evidences that it's from God. Number two, that it's preserved.", "Now, when a Christian comes and says to me: the Bible, I'm going to follow it, and everything it says is true, I'll ask them, first: bring me proofs that the Bible is from God. Number two, you agree yourself, if you look at your Christian scholars, that your book is corrupted. So you cannot apply the same analogy now. You cannot now make it the same with Islam and Christianity and Judaism, when one has a book that is preserved and has evidences from God, and two don't. Therefore, yes, anything that disagrees with the words of God, after proving and establishing the words of God, is false.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Niqabi Challenges the Continuity of Islam with Previous Scriptures! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7-kSmD09rxI", ((1723, "28:43–28:55"), (1763, "29:23–29:44"), (1784, "29:44–30:30"),), id: 950)

