#passage(("I've already established that we cannot say that the gospels are reliable. But our main question was about what evidence Christianity is the truth. Even if I were to accept this idea, let me hypothetically accept the gospels are reliable: that's not evidence that Christianity is true. If someone writing a history in a book, it doesn't mean it happened. Even if I were to accept the gospels, you have to prove the gospels themselves have some sort of evidence that they're from God. If you just say: okay, they're writing history, the history could have been true or false. People writing history in a book, it doesn't mean Christianity is true.", "And then I'll add you another layer, which is that the gospels, or the Bible, doesn't teach what Christians today believe. So basically it's layers of falsehood upon each other: it's not reliable, but even if it was reliable, it doesn't prove that the information in it is true. And even if we accept it's reliable and the information in it is true, there's nothing in it that talks about the Trinity or Jesus being divine. So how many layers of conceding do I need to do to show you that there is no such thing as evidence [for] Christianity?",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Agnostic Puts Islam And Christianity To The Test! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7qT2I7lBW18", ((853, "14:13–14:46"), (886, "14:46–15:19"),), id: 952)
