#passage(("For instance, you say you arrive to God. What is God? Who is God? This is a part of what we say knowing what the truth is: you need to identify who the creator is. So we say you humble yourself before God. Of course, that's what being a Muslim is about; this is the essence of being a Muslim: submission. Submit and humbling yourself in front of the creator, that's what being a Muslim is. So we agree on that. But first we need to know what God is. If you think God is a human being, if a person thinks God is a cow, if another person thinks God is a son, these things are not God. God is not the son, God is not a cow. So we need to first identify what God is. This is a part of knowing what objectively the truth is.", "In many of my discussions, this is something I ask Christians usually: give me one evidence that Christianity is the truth, which is a challenge that I make to everyone. I say: you're a Hindu, you're a seeker or whatever, you need to be able to produce some evidence, or to prove that what you believe in is the truth. Allah says in the Quran that the Jews and the Christians, they said: if you're a Jew, you're going to enter heaven. If you're a Christian, you're going to enter heaven. If not, you're not going to enter heaven. So Allah says in the Quran: produce your proofs if you're truthful. So this is what it all comes down to.", "So when I speak to someone, I say: okay, you're a Christian, you believe Christianity is the truth, perfect, go ahead and give me one compelling reason. And before you speak, I'm going to give you some caveats, because I deal with a lot of Christians and they always do this. So the caveat number one: it cannot be personal experience. You cannot say to me: I was sleeping, and Jesus came to me in my dream and he hugged me, and I was a drug addict and I stopped being a drug addict. Okay, cool, but that's a personal experience. Truth needs to be accessible to everyone. I need to be able to present it to someone today. It cannot be something that happened in the past that nobody can verify. Your own personal experiences do not count. You got to present something that is objectively true: if we use reasoning and common sense and investigate that thing, [we] come to the conclusion this must be the truth coming from God. What is the thing that you can present to an atheist, to someone who's not a Christian, to show that Christianity is the truth? Don't tell me general statements and stuff like that.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “The Muslim Lantern, Sneako and Arab Debate Religion! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QiBVA3ZecoI", ((294, "4:54–5:36"), (338, "5:38–6:42"), (402, "6:42–7:58"),), id: 956)
