#passage(("The difference between me and you is, what I did was: let me investigate Islam and see the evidences that objectively make it true. Even though I already liked the faith, meaning that when I was young, I used to like the information that Islam used to say, because it made sense and it was applicable to the reality around me. And I actually used to understand the Quran; I used to find it very fascinating, even when I was younger. That's the difference between me and you as well: you were reading the Bible when you were young, it didn't make sense, or you were not deep enough to understand the information. But for me, the Quran is that text that you would understand, it doesn't matter what your age is. When you're young, if you're able to read and comprehend on a basic level, the Quran will still be very deep for you. It was very deep for me when I was reading it. I used to like to listen to the Quran and read it.", "But still, I did not let that bias make me say: okay, the materialistic world is not going to do anything for me, so let me just become Muslim and follow Islam. I said: no, let me investigate what objectively proves that Islam is the truth, then let me investigate other religions and see what they put forward to be the truth. So I would say the difference between my experience and yours is: the end result was based on objective evidence versus subjective experience. Because you had a subjective experience; you called it maybe the Holy Spirit, and then you saw Scripture in a completely different way when you were reading. So that is a subjective experience.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Claims He Studied Islam For 12 Years?! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gvPZJMH0co4", ((77, "1:17–2:02"), (122, "2:02–2:43"),), id: 957)
