#passage(("The reason you can know why Islam is true or not true is the evidences that Islam came with, or Prophet Muhammad came with. Now, if someone comes and says: OK, the Christians also claim the religion is true, we will ask: OK, where is the objective evidence that Christians have that validates their faith to be from God? Now, that claim can be applied to any religion. And whatever religion has evidence, which are objective, that can be presented, that this person was a Messenger of God, is the religion that is ought to be followed. It's as simple as that.", "You're coming back to repeat the fallacy of generalisation. You don't know what proofs Muslims have. You're just saying nobody has the objective evidence. You're not asking, you're making a claim. If I say \"nobody has milk\", that's not a question. It's a claim I'm making, that nobody possesses this specific thing. If you're asking why is the proof in a specific religion, that is a question. And I've already told you: every religion should present evidence.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Heated Atheist Demands Muslim To Prove His Faith! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=L9Kzj4FZCcc", ((503, "8:23–8:54"), (540, "9:00–9:35"),), id: 958)
