#passage(("Now, you said you believe it because it makes sense to you. The teaching makes sense to you. Like I said to you, anything you presented already exists in Islam. And I would ask you to tell me: what is there of a great teaching of Christianity that so inspired you so much that doesn't exist in Islam? Because if you don't have an answer to that question, then you cannot say: oh, these teachings are great. Because if they exist in other faith as well, then it doesn't prove Christianity to be true.", "Now, you said: praying every day in the name of Jesus. Jesus didn't tell anyone to pray every day in the name of Jesus; that doesn't exist. The religion that teaches to pray every day is Islam. You're applying an Islamic practice and then saying that changed my life. We say: yes, we agree with you. Welcome to Islam and his teachings. Yes, you should pray every day. Purify yourself. You connect with God. Not just on a Sunday, \"go and visit the church if you feel like it\". That's not the teachings of God, but that's what Christians do. So you're telling us what Islam teaches, and saying that it is what Christianity teaches, and it is not the case.", "Then you're saying: \"My life was a total mess\", and all of that. That's what every Christian comes up with. Your life can change with something false. It doesn't have to be true because your life changed and you convince yourself that this is everything.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Convert Attempts To Convince A Muslim Of Christianity! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rsp5eGYtL3Y", ((811, "13:31–14:18"), (858, "14:18–14:52"), (892, "14:52–15:06"),), id: 966)
