#passage(("No one can argue against emotional things. I can bring you now hundred of Muslims with a similar story, but rather than calling upon Jesus, they called upon Allah. I can bring a hundred Hindus that, rather than calling upon Allah or Jesus, they called upon Krishna. Does that make, therefore, their beliefs true, just because they called upon something and then they got that thing happening? And it's not hard to find these stories. If you just go on YouTube and you click any religion and you click \"experience\", you'll have people talking about their experience, and very genuine. You will know it's genuine because you will see it's not faked. But in the end, can this just personal experience that I had in my life be a criteria for what is true and what is false?", "And when you said you called upon Jesus, did you know any other gods to call upon anyways? That's what you were raised upon! If you're raised upon something, you would naturally call upon that which you're raised upon, what you identify yourself with. So if you genuinely thought Jesus was God and you called upon God for help, Allah helps the people who are in need. If you did not know who the true God is, the only thing you knew was Jesus, and you genuinely thought he was God, it wouldn't make any sense for Allah to expect you to call upon something else, because you do not know anything else. You only know Jesus.", "If you sincerely call upon Allah, that's something well known in Islamic literature. In fact, Allah says in the Quran (Luqman31:32): (when they are in the sea and the waves are like Mountain, they call upon Allah). They call upon God sincerely, Allah means God, (and then when Allah saves them and they go to the shore, they start associating partners with Him again) (Al'ankabut29:65). In the point of sincerity, in the point of need, you'll call upon Allah sincerely, you will call upon God: \"God help me\", and then God helped you, and then in the end you come back to associating partners with him, when it's times of ease now, when things are OK.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Does Jesus Possess The Attributes of God?! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2Jp6DQffnZg", ((315, "5:15–5:54"), (374, "6:14–6:47"), (413, "6:53–7:22"),), id: 970)
