#passage(("How can you evangelize to me then, if what you're going to bring up is not going to satisfy the people who are not Christians? Then how can you convince them of your faith? I've been talking with Christians for a while. For the whole time I've been talking to Christians, they've been trying to evangelize, even praying for me, trying to heal things that I don't have problems with. Anyways, they've tried to do all these things; why isn't the holy spirit working? You just said that it's through the holy spirit you get guided. I've read the Bible. What is more than that in seeking God, by reading the Scripture of God?", "And when I read the Bible, by the way, I was not reading it from an Islamic lens, trying to find mistakes. I was genuinely reading it, trying to see where these people are coming from. Because when you are Muslim, then you're always curious about the differences between Islam and Christianity, and you want to see: OK, why do these people believe these things that we don't believe in? And then when I read the Bible, I saw it actually supports what we believe in, instead of what the Christians believe in. So I was even more confused: why do these people believe in the things they believe in? And then I realized that all of this comes from the Church. All of this comes after the Romans adopted Christianity, spread this religion in churches, and the people adopted this religion, father and son and son and son, until today. And it has nothing to do with what the Bible says. There are no explicit verses regarding the Trinity.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Attempts To Convert Muslim! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=s7wX-huScq0", ((493, "8:13–9:12"), (563, "9:23–10:03"),), id: 971)
