#passage(("Each one of you should ask himself: Why are you a Muslim? Is it because you're born a Muslim? That's what the كفار قريش (Disbelievers of Quraysh) said! (alMaida5:104): قَالُوا۟ حَسْبُنَا مَا وَجَدْنَا عَلَيْهِ ءَابَآءَنَآ (That's what we found our forefathers upon) أَوَلَوْ كَانَ ءَابَآؤُهُمْ لَا يَعْلَمُونَ شَيْـًۭٔا وَلَا يَهْتَدُونَ (What if their forefathers they know nothing, they were not people of intellect and knowledge). So why are you a Muslim? The answer should be: \"I'm a Muslim because ISLAM IS THE TRUTH\". Islam is the حقّ Haqq (Truth). (alKahf18:29) فَمَن شَآءَ فَلْيُؤْمِن وَمَن شَآءَ فَلْيَكْفُرْ (Who wishes to believe, let him believe. And who wishes to disbelieve, let him disbelieve). Liberalism? No! إِنَّآ أَعْتَدْنَا لِلظَّـٰلِمِينَ نَارًا أَحَاطَ بِهِمْ سُرَادِقُهَا (We have prepared for the disbelievers a Hellfire that will surround them). So, Allah is not saying: who wishes to believe, believe, and who wishes to disbelieve, disbelieve. What Allah said is a warning! It's like when you have a child, and then you say: \"Yeah! OK! Do it! Watch the TV! Do it!\" Does that mean you're telling him to watch the TV? No! You're warning him. So Allah is warning; He's saying: Yes, you want to disbelieve, disbelieve, but this is the outcome.", "Once you understand this is the Haqq, then we need to know: Why we are Muslims? What are the evidences for Islam? Why do you believe that Prophet Muhammadﷺ is a Messenger of Allah? Why is the Quran the True Message from God? You need to know those things. You need to absorb them.", "It's not boastful, but I want to say it: even if you were to bring me a 100 of the smartest Atheists today, and they stand here, whatever they say is not going to change the fact that I know this is from Allah. Why? Because the amount of evidences that I saw, it becomes IMPOSSIBLE for this not to be the Haqq. A lame human being, no matter how smart he thinks he is, when he comes from a sperm drop, whatever he utters is not going to influence that which I have as a foundation, which is unshakable. It is inconceivable, impossible, for the things that Islam put forward as evidence not for it to be the Truth. Just like you see the Sun: if I bring a 100 Atheists, would they convince you there's no Sun? Would they convince you that we're not speaking right now? Same way -you know for a fact that you're speaking right now- Islam is the Truth. This Quran is Haqq. Not \"probably it's Haqq, like some people say, I heard that..\" No, It is the Haqq, Certainty! وَكَانُوا۟ بِـَٔايَـٰتِنَا يُوقِنُونَ (They are certain about our verses) (As–Sajdah32:24). This is يقيّن (Yaqeen: Certainty): you have Yaqeen that this Deen is from Allahﷻ, from a knowledge level. But there are levels of Yaqeen. The second level is to see, عينُ اليقيّن. We've not seen! And حقُّ اليقيّن is to experience it. We've not experienced Jannah (Paradise) and Nar (Hellfire) and Jinn (Another Creation of God). But we are at the first level: you have علمُ اليقيّن, knowledge for certainty that this is from Allahﷻ. So this is what you need. You need to know why you're a Muslim.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “The Situation Of The Ummah, The Disease & The Cure | Al Muwahiddeen Mosque - The Netherlands |”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0ycNKKOx2jg", ((3681, "1:01:21–1:02:35"), (3761, "1:02:41–1:02:58"), (3784, "1:03:04–1:04:45"),), id: 1017)
