#passage(("For instance, prophecies of the future: that's one example. We know that human beings do not know absolute future; they do not know what's going to happen. We are bound by the time space continuum that we live in in the universe.", "Another type is the knowledge of the natural world -I don't use the term scientific for them- Allah describing the natural world, because He's describing them objectively, the way they are. They cannot change; they are the way Allah said they will be. So you have Allah describing expansion of the universe (adhDhariyat51:47), describing embryology (alMuminun23:12-14), describing many, many different things that the Quran talks about.", "You have another example: history, things which the Prophetﷺ did not know. It is not information known in the civilizations in his time. For example, when the Quran talks about the ancient Egyptian beliefs, like Pharaoh claiming to be God (anNaziat79:24), or ancient Mesopotamia: we did not read [hieroglyphics] until we discovered the Rosetta Stone in 1799 or 1899, which is like 2, 3 hundred years ago. We couldn't even read [hieroglyphics]; we couldn't read what the Egyptians believed. Even if you went to Egypt and you tried to study the pyramids, you'll not be able to understand.", "Another example, the life of the Prophetﷺ himself. What would be the reasons, the motives for him to lie? If he wasn't saying the truth, you have to give me other explanations. Was he lying? Was he delusional? The Prophet is far from any of these accusations. Why was he doing what he was doing? You'll have to provide us with a rational explanation.", "Another example is the laws of the Quran, the Prophetﷺ brings in the Quran and Hadith: the social laws, how to run the community, society, how to deal with finances, the punitive laws, all of these things that cannot come from that desert Bedouin Arabian, Prophet Muhammadﷺ.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Ex-Muslim Claims The Quran Is Full Of Scientific Mistakes?! Muhammed Al