#passage(("You investigate any claim, and using that, you come to the conclusion whether something is true or false.", "Another evidence is that the Prophet talked about the past. What past? The past that he didn't know, meaning his community didn't know, because he was in the Deserts of Arabia. They had a very limited set of knowledge. For example, the Prophetﷺ talked about Abraham and people in Ancient Mesopotamia. The Sumerian language was dead at the time of the Prophetﷺ, at the time of Jesus as well, and the temple that had this information is called the Ziggurat of Ur, and it was buried under the sand. It was not discovered. So the Prophet could not access the language or the temple that had the artifact that has the information, but the Quran mentions information that we discovered after the Prophet. So, there are many things like this in the Quran.", "Another form of evidence is the life of the Prophet himself. We have an idea of testimony: what he did, that people testified, saw what he did, and continuously transmitted information about him, his life; studying the motivations of why he was doing what he was doing.", "Another evidence is the social structure of Islam, the teachings of Islam, which do deal with every aspect of life: social laws, government laws, financial laws. Things that cannot come from one man, because you cannot be an expert in all of these different fields. There are multiple different evidences that we combine together. And of course, the most important is the Quran itself, and no one being able to imitate it in the Arabic language. It's a very unique scripture; it has always been that unique scripture. This is how we know for a FACT that Islam is the Truth.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Anonymous Atheist Attempts To Outsmart A Muslim! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WC2nmWKjHVQ", ((1061, "17:41–17:43"), (1115, "18:35–19:46"), (1199, "19:59–20:11"), (1241, "20:41–21:23"),), id: 1023)
