#passage(("When it comes to studying Islam, Islam is not something that someone can spend a few years and learn. For example, you have a scholar called Sheikh Al-Albani, who's from Albania, and he spent his whole life studying one field of Islam, which was the science of Hadith. So, Islam is such a vast sea, and the encyclopaedia of Islam and religious scriptures are beyond the understanding of anyone. And if you don't have even the tools to learn it and study it, like the Arabic language, for example, and the basic tools to dig into the text and understand it, I wouldn't say I have studied Islam. You can say \"Yes, I've studied Islam to a specific level\", \"I've studied some things, I've read this and that\", but the evidences of Islam are so many.", "When it comes to you saying that \"Islam came 600 years...\": if something comes 10,000 years after something else, it doesn't change the fact that it's true or false, if it comes from the same source, which is God. Christians believe in the New Testament, which comes thousands of years after the Old Testament. It doesn't change the fact that they believe both of them came from God, and therefore both of them are accurate and correct. The scriptures that people believe in today, of the Old Testament, it includes things which were revealed to Noah, it includes things which were revealed to Abraham, things that came thousands and thousands of years before the New Testament.", "God has something called progressive Revelation: He sends Prophets progressively. He sends Adam, He sent Noah, He sent Abraham, then you have David, Solomon, Moses, and then you have Jesus. God sends Prophets one after the other. So, of course, there will be a time difference between the Prophets that are sent between one and the other. Now, that doesn't change the reality that they're all from God and they're all true; and the history, the difference when one was revealed and one wasn't, does not change that reality or fact. So that's not an argument, because it can apply to you when it comes to the Old Testament. It can apply to you with other religions that claim they're older, like Hinduism will tell you \"We're 5,000 years old\", or whatever, one of the oldest religions. You get many people that will claim that. Something being older than something doesn't mean anything.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “77 Year Old Christian Veteran Attempts To Convert A Muslim! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ELmBcT8w0qI", ((743, "12:23–13:08"), (800, "13:20–13:54"), (844, "14:04–14:46"),), id: 1127)
