#passage(("Why is the Sabbath not a part of the Islamic religion? It's not part of the Christian religion as well. Christians of today, the majority, over 90% of them: their day of worship is Sunday, which the church has actually innovated, this idea of Sunday being the day of worship, because there's nothing in the Bible that says that you have to worship on Sunday. But this is the tradition of the church; this is what has become predominant for Christians. So Christians don't really keep the Sabbath. Even if you want to come from a Christian point of view: Christians claim something called Progressive Revelation (we believe in it as well): that Revelation and the commands of God change with time based on the needs of the people. So the teachings of Noah were not the same as the teachings of Moses, and the teachings of Moses are not the same as the teachings of Jesus. The teachings of Jesus are not the same as the teachings of Prophet Muhammadﷺ.", "Allahﷻ affirms that there is something called Sabbath. Allah affirms that in the Quran, and He says that the Children of Israel have transgressed in the Sabbath (Albaqara2:65) \"الَّذِينَ اعْتَدَوْا مِنكُمْ فِي السَّبْتِ\": that they were working on the Sabbath even though they were not supposed to work on the Sabbath, but they were trying to play games with God. They put the net on Friday night, and then the fish go in the net on Saturday, and they stay home, they don't do anything. On Sunday then they collect the fish. They were playing games with God: \"We didn't really do fishing on Saturday\" (Ala'raf7:163). Because God was testing them: God was bringing a lot of fish on Saturday to test them; on the other days of the week there were not as many fish. So what happened is that they were always seeing fish on Saturday, and they know Saturday they cannot work; that's the test. So what they used to do is trying to trick God. But Allahﷻ affirms something called the Sabbath, and he says that it was made upon those who transgressed on it (Annahl16:24). So it's not an obligation for everyone; it was an obligation for the Children of Israel at that time. And it is certainly not for God resting on the Seventh Day! (Gen2:1-3) God does not rest, He does not need energy, He does not need refreshment as Human Beings. If God needed to rest, He wouldn't be God.", "So from an Islamic perspective, we believe the teachings of all Prophets are the same, meaning that they tell you to worship One God and to follow the Messenger of your time. But those Messengers bring different Laws for the People, and they don't all behave the same way: Allahﷻ says in the Quran that Children of Israel have transgressed a lot (Albaqara2:40-103), and the Bible mentions the same thing (Joshua7:11-12). They disobeyed God even though He showed them so many signs (Albaqara2:211). So God made things difficult for them by increasing the commands on them, because they were a transgressing Nation (Alan'am6:146). But those commands Muslims are not obliged to follow, because this is not the same Nation; we did not do these things.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Muslim Highlights The Inconsistency Of The Bible! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KcRdd8LsvKE", ((35, "0:35–1:29"), (92, "1:32–2:34"), (159, "2:39–3:18"),), id: 1128)
