#passage(("The prophets teach the same beliefs. So, then we have two things now: we have beliefs, and we have Sharia, which is the laws that are applicable to the people at the time. Now, the beliefs are always the same: there's one God, there's angels, there's heaven, hellfire, all of these things. The beliefs of the prophets were always the same: worship God alone, do not associate partners with him. It's the same message. But when it comes to the Sharia now, the legal teachings and things, do's and don'ts, this can change from time to time. People are different in a different community, in a different society, in a different time: God will give them a different teaching in that case, in these legal binding things, that befits them the most.", "So, these prophets were sent to their nations only. They were not sent for everyone. Prophet Muhammad was last and final messenger for everyone. So, he needed this guidance that works for everyone.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Agnostic Claims That Pantheism Is More Rational Than Monotheism! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=C3BXt0zJr3o", ((1446, "24:06–24:51"), (1493, "24:53–25:00"),), id: 1129)
