#passage(("At the time of Joseph (who was a Messenger of God), in his time, people were allowed to prostrate to human beings out of respect. But we believe that that command is abrogated today: the Prophet Muhammad said you shouldn't prostrate to anyone, any human being, because we believe in progressive Revelation, and God gives different commands based on what people are receptive to, based on their condition as well.", "So when you talk about water and wine: first, we do not believe there's any historical evidence this happened, number one. Number 2, assuming it happened, we can always say, if this was true, that there were different laws for those different people. Perhaps they were allowed to drink a little bit, but at their Sharia and their own legislative laws. So it doesn't really cause a problem for us from an Islamic point of view. Just like you see Jesus: he had certain commands that he broke from the Jewish tradition, and the Jews were not happy. So he had some progressive Revelation things. For example, if you go to (Matthew15:1-2): washing your hands before you eat, or something related to that; the Jewish people had an issue with him not keeping that command. These are basic things that he might have broken, but the main things he kept, the Jewish teachings. But there are examples of him doing things like this. So there are certain commands that can be abrogated, and there is progressive Revelation.", "And Christians have to believe in Progressive Revelations anyway, because they don't follow the 613 laws.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Family Grills Muslim On His Beliefs! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TKqmYTyocyo", ((984, "16:24–16:53"), (1018, "16:58–18:03"), (1083, "18:03–18:07"),), id: 1131)
