#passage(("If the Bible has been changed, and there is one God, and Jesus was a messenger of God, God is also going to send us other Messengers to guide us to the truth, so he can also keep us guided, because if the message is corrupted and changed, then how can people determine what is from God, what is not from God? Doesn't God need to send us another messenger, so we can be upon Clarity when it comes to truth and falsehood?", "As Muslims, we believe in the previous Messengers: we believe in Moses, Noah, Abraham, Jesus, and we believe Prophet Muhammad, peace be upon Him, is also a messenger that was sent in the line of these Messengers. And Allah, whenever the message was corrupted by people, or the beliefs of people are corrupted, Allah will send the messengers so he can bring people back to the truth, because people, for their own desires, corrupt messages. So Allah sent Prophet Muhammad after Jesus for that reason.", "If you look at the earliest group of Christianity, the [Ebionites], the nazarians, etc., there's many groups that very early, that today they will call heretic, they will call bad Christians or not real Christian, but they believed in one God and they believe Jesus was sent by God; they didn't believe in a trinity or any of that. So what happened is the religion corrupted later. So 325 you had the Council of [Nicaea], 381 you had the Council of Constantinople; then they brought the trinity in. This is when they changed the Bible and changed the beliefs. So they introduced Jesus, he become God all of a sudden, one of three, etc.", "So Prophet Muhammad came with what you believe: there is one Creator, not 3 in one; that Jesus is a messenger of God, like you believe that he's also messenger of God; that we should worship God Alone; these were Messengers all sent by the Creator, Noah, Abraham, all of these; and that this is now the teaching that is relevant to your day and time. Teachings change. Prophet Muhammad, Allah sent him with a universal message to everywhere, cuz one message is enough for everyone. So then Allah preserved the Quran for that reason. So unlike the changes that you say that happen in the Bible, Allah made sure that the Quran is preserved. How do you know the truth if he's not going to send a messenger? The message has to be preserved, so then you can learn about how to connect to the Creator, how to follow guidance, how to avoid misguidance, etc.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Sincere Lady About To Accept Islam But This Happens! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=V2bQy_K4u5g", ((77, "1:17–1:45"), (108, "1:48–2:12"), (132, "2:12–2:47"), (167, "2:47–3:57"),), id: 1177)
