#passage(("If you die rejecting one of the messengers of God, you don't go to paradise, but after hearing the message: you hear the message, you investigate, you see the evidences, and then you'll die rejecting it. It is the same God: the God of Abraham is the God of prophet Muhammad.", "The Bible, it's not sufficient. It is not sufficient for two reasons. First, it's been changed by people: different Bibles, different versions, which are not all the same. Number two is God has intended it to the children of Israel, the new and old testament. When I say it's not sufficient, is because times change: the commands of God is gradual. When Jesus rose from the dead, according to the Bible, he said: go and [preach] all nations. And this verse, a lot of the Christian scholars say it's interpolation. It's a corruption. He says to them: baptize in the name of the father, son, and the holy spirit. But the problem is none of the disciples ever baptized in the name of the father, son. We have the acts of the apostles after Jesus. How did they baptize? In the name of Jesus only. Because if he commanded them baptizing in the name of the father, son and the holy spirit, we will find at least one disciple doing that. That's why you have a lot of scholars saying that this verse is a change, is an addition, as many other verses in the bible.", "But just like you didn't say the Old Testament was sufficient, because it's the same God, and you follow the New Testament, you should follow the last testament and also say that you follow the God's progressive revelation. If he wants to send another prophet, he does, cuz times change and people's needs change and people's commands change. God had many restrictions for the children of Israel because they were disobedient. You don't have the same restrictions because you're not from the same children of Israel. And Allah mentions that in the Quran.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Muslim And Educated Christian Debate The Divinity Of Jesus Christ! Muha