#passage(("The Prophet Muhammad coming 600 years later: that is not a problem at all. Why is it not a problem at all? Because Prophet Muhammad is not coming to talk about Jesus's life. This is what Christians are not understanding. Prophet Muhammad is a new Messenger of God sent to bring a new Revelation. He's coming to deliver a Message of God, just like Jesus came hundreds of years after Isaiah, for example, and Isaiah came hundreds of years after Moses, and Moses came hundreds of years after Abraham, and Abraham came hundreds of years after Noah. Prophets of God come progressively, hundreds of years, one after the other. They don't come to talk about the previous Prophet. They come to bring Revelation progressively from God, from the same source, which is the Creator.", "So what you should be asking, if you talk about historicity, is: the manuscripts that talk about Prophet Muhammad, for example, what is their dating? Or the Quran, what is his dating in relation to Prophet Muhammad? This is what you're supposed to ask. What you cannot ask is that Prophet Muhammad came 600 years after Jesus, as if Prophet Muhammad is sent by Jesus or something, or he's coming to tell you the life of Jesus. He's not! He comes from the same God, which is the God of Jesus.", "I'm not comparing the Quran, or what Prophet Muhammad said, to the Gospels, because they are two different scripts that talk about different things. The New Testament is supposed to talk about the life of Jesus, and the teachings about Jesus. But the Quran, or the Message of Prophet Muhammad, is not to talk about the life of Jesus, or what he did or what he didn't do. It's not like the writings of the Bible. You're comparing apples and oranges. It's like me saying: oh, this manuscript that talks about Moses comes these many years before this manuscript that talks about Jesus. But they're talking about different people; there's no relationship there! The second thing is, you are the one who's supposed to bring evidence. You are saying Jesus said this, and then you have a manuscript that is 400 years after him, written by unknown people, meaning we don't have a reason to trust that.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Questions The Reliability Of The Quran Then It Backfires! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PkLmuzqRqPU", ((860, "14:20–15:04"), (909, "15:09–15:33"), (1019, "16:59–17:58"),), id: 1179)
