#passage(("All the Prophets are examples for us. And in fact Allah says in the (Quran6:90) to Prophet Muhammad to follow the way of all the Prophets. After Allah mentioned the Prophets, he said أُولَٰئِكَ الَّذِينَ هَدَى اللَّهُ \"those are the ones that Allah guided\" فَبِهُدَاهُمُ اقْتَدِهْ \"so follow their guidance\". And also Allah عزوجل says: ثُمَّ أَوْحَيْنَا إِلَيْكَ أَنِ اتَّبِعْ مِلَّةَ إِبْرَاهِيمَ حَنِيفًا \"Follow the Monotheistic Path of Abraham\", \"And do not be of the polytheists\" وَمَا كَانَ مِنَ ٱلْمُشْرِكِينَ (Quran16:123). So Allah commands the Prophet to follow the way of the Messengers, because all of the Messengers came with the same Message when it comes to monotheism. They came sometimes with different teachings in the practicality of the society, because societies were different. But the teachings about God and beliefs were always the same: there's one God, One Creator, there is Angels, there is Hellfire, there is Paradise, Etc.", "Prophets can make mistakes; they can make minor sins. Noah asked Allah to save his son, but his son's disbelieved and disobeyed. So Allah عزوجل corrected him; he said to him: he's not from your Family. Then he asked for forgiveness (Quran11:46-47).", "Musa عليه السلام (Moses): there were two people fighting, one from his tribe and one from the enemy tribe. So the one that is from the same tribe as Musa عليه السلام, he asked for help; he said: aid me, help me. So Musa عليه السلام came and he just pushed the guy, but Musa عليه السلام was very strong. He did not try to kill him; he pushed him, the other person fell and died. So here Musa عليه السلام committed what can be considered a minor sin, because unintentional. Then he straight away asked for forgiveness. He said this is from the work of Satan, and then he asked Allah to forgive him (Quran28:15-16). Certain things for a Prophet can be a mistake, for us not a mistake, because they are held to so much higher regard.", "Another example: Musa عليه السلام -but this is not considered really a sin- he was asked who's the most knowledgeable person on Earth? And he said: me! But he was a Mighty Messenger of God. He was one of the 5 main Messengers of God, getting direct revelation, so he's not [boasting] by saying this. But then Allah revealed to him: no you're not, go to our servant called الخضر (Alkhidr) and learn from him.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Agnostic Challenges Muslim On God Then This Happens! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MSk1AiEaXH8", ((1410, "23:30–24:08"), (1457, "24:17–26:16"), (1588, "26:28–27:21"), (1646, "27:26–27:46"),), id: 1183)
